// TEST: Two caret variables meeting by arithmetic, Int64 and Float64 elements (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3019 @ 8:22
// ERROR-CONTAINS: must agree EXACTLY
// `a + b` was typed as `T`, so this instance typed the Float64 sum Int64 and
// g++ refused the narrowing (BL9002, an internal error) -- the unification
// that makes two bare generic variables one skips carets. The elements meet,
// so they must agree; the caller writes `adda(Float64([1, 2]), ...)`.
function adda(a: T^1, b: U^1) = a + b
let r = adda([1, 2], [0.5, 0.5])
